# UUID registration table and drain-before-reuse discipline

Models `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer`'s UUID-keyed session map `sessions_`
(`flat_hash_map<uint64_t, SessionEntry>`, each entry a
`SessionEntry {session, req_id, role}` holding the decode consumer's receive
sessions and the prefill producer's send offers alike — the request id a
session is reported under lives in the entry, not in the session) and
its terminal report sets (`done_sending_`, `done_recving_`, `failed_recving_`)
across duplicate announcements, conflicting UUIDs, and session retries
(`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::NotifyForRead`,
`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::StartRead(remote_endpoint)`,
`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::RegisterRecv` / `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked`,
`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::RetireSettledSessionLocked`,
`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::CompleteReadWithDetails`,
`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::CompleteReadRaw` in
`tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer.cc`,
`SendLifecycleTest.DuplicateRegistrationCannotReplaceLiveOffer`,
`RecvDrainTest.DuplicateUuidIsRejectedUntilExpiredReceiveDrains`,
`RecvLifecycleTest.RegisterRecvFinishesAReadyIncumbentBeforeReplacingIt` and
`RecvLifecycleTest.RedeliveredStartReadLeavesAReadyReceiveToCompleteRead` in
`tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer_send_drain_test.cc`, and
`ControlHandshakeTest.DuplicateReceiveDoesNotReplaceOrLeakFirstRead` and
`ControlHandshakeTest.RepeatedReceiveAnnouncementIsIdempotent` in
`tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer_control_test.cc`).

The model keeps the one map as two tables indexed by uuid, `recvTable` and
`sendTable`, so that each entry carries its own session model (`Recv`, `Send`)
next to its `reqId` (`SessionEntry::req_id`); every event that seats an entry
first consults the other table, so no uuid is ever held in both
(`violatesExclusive`, bounded), and the pair reads as `sessions_`.

Abbreviations: `mgr.h` / `mgr.cc` =
`tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer.{h,cc}`, `recv.h` / `recv.cc` =
