## Protocol rules encoded

1. **Consumer `StartRead(req_id, uuid, ...)` (`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::StartRead(remote_endpoint)`):**
   - `auto incumbent = sessions_.find(uuid)`; if there is one,
     `RetireSettledSessionLocked(incumbent)` retires it when it is `Done()` and
     otherwise returns false, whatever kind of session it is:
     - a **receive with the same `req_id`** (the entry's `incumbent_req_id == req_id`):
       idempotent re-announcement — returns without allocating staging,
       replacing the incumbent, finishing it, or recording a failure
       (`ControlHandshakeTest.RepeatedReceiveAnnouncementIsIdempotent`,
       `RecvLifecycleTest.RedeliveredStartReadLeavesAReadyReceiveToCompleteRead`);
     - a **receive with a different `req_id`**, or a **send offer**
       (`recv_incumbent == nullptr`): rejects the duplicate — leaves the
       incumbent untouched, allocates no staging slot, and records the new
       `req_id` in `failed_recving_` with an `AlreadyExistsError`
       (`ControlHandshakeTest.DuplicateReceiveDoesNotReplaceOrLeakFirstRead`).
   - A settled incumbent (`Done()`) is retired inline — a receive into
     `done_recving_` / `failed_recving_` (if it `tracks_completion()`), a send
     offer into `done_sending_` / `failed_recving_` — and erased before the new
     session is created and seated by `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked`.

2. **Consumer `RegisterRecv` → `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked(uuid, req_id, session)`
   (`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::RegisterRecv`,
   `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::EmplaceRecvSessionLocked`):**
   - If `sessions_[uuid]` holds a receive that is `!IsDraining()` and
     `IsReadyToComplete()`, it is finished first (`recv->Finish()`, the
     model's `Recv.pollReady`); then `RetireSettledSessionLocked` retires the
     entry if it is `Done()` — a receive or a settled send offer alike. A
     ready incumbent with nothing in flight is settled by that finish and
     replaced in the same call
     (`RecvLifecycleTest.RegisterRecvFinishesAReadyIncumbentBeforeReplacingIt`).
   - `try_emplace` of `SessionEntry{session, req_id, SessionRole::kTransfer}`
     then fails with `AlreadyExistsError` on any entry still present: a receive that is draining with work in flight (including one the
     finish just started draining), or a live send offer. The rejected
     candidate is dropped by its creator and its staging goes with it
     (`TransferReceiveSession::~TransferReceiveSession` → `ReleaseStaging()`),
     keeping the incumbent authoritative until its in-flight operations finish
     (`RecvDrainTest.DuplicateUuidIsRejectedUntilExpiredReceiveDrains`).
   - `RegisterActivePlan` seats its receive through the same
     `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked`. Because every `TransferSession::plan()`
     implementation (`TransferReceiveSession::plan`, `TransferSendSession::plan`,
     `ReshardSendSession::plan`, `ReshardReceiveSession::plan`) returns
     `absl::nullopt` once `Done()` is `true`, the up-front check
     `existing->second.session->plan().has_value()` refuses any *unsettled*
     (`!Done()`) plan-carrying incumbent with `AlreadyExistsError` — including a
     ready-to-complete plan-carrying receive, without finishing it — whereas a
     *settled* (`Done()`) plan-carrying incumbent returns `nullopt` from `plan()`
     and falls through to `RetireSettledSessionLocked` like any other settled
     session; its `is_sender` arm seats a send session the same way. Neither arm is a
     separate event here: `registerRecv` is `RegisterRecv` (and the white-box
     fixture `RecvTestManager::AddRecv`, which writes `sessions_[uuid]`
     directly, as a `SessionEntry`, with `acquire_staging = true`; the slot `registerRecv` takes
     models that and `RegisterActivePlan` under dynamic staging — production
     `RegisterRecv` passes `acquire_staging = false` and takes none).

3. **Producer `NotifyForRead(req_id, uuid, ...)` (`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::NotifyForRead`):**
   - `sessions_.try_emplace(uuid, SessionEntry{session, req_id, SessionRole::kTransfer})`
     rejects any `uuid` the map already holds — a live or settled send offer, or a live or settled receive — as a
     thrown `std::runtime_error`; `NotifyForRead` retires nothing
     (`SendLifecycleTest.DuplicateRegistrationCannotReplaceLiveOffer`). The
     model's `none` is that rejection.

4. **Sweep in `CompleteReadWithDetails()` / `CompleteReadRaw()`
   (`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::CompleteReadWithDetails`,
   `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::CompleteReadRaw`):**
   - Every entry of `sessions_` goes through `RetireSettledSessionLocked`:
     only sessions with `Done()` (`done = true`) are reported, under the
     entry's `req_id`, into `done_sending_` / `done_recving_` /
     `failed_recving_` and erased. Before that, the sweep polls a receive that
     is `!IsDraining()` (`recv->IsReadyToComplete()` → `recv->Finish()`) and
     fails any session of any kind past its deadline
     (`session->deadline() <= now`), which are `recvStep` / `sendStep` events
     here. (A send
     session registered by `RegisterActivePlan` is instead erased unreported by
     `UnregisterActivePlan` before it is finished, `sessions_.erase(it);` —
     outside this model, whose sends are `NotifyForRead` offers.)

## Lock scopes

`sessions_`, `done_sending_`, `done_recving_`, and `failed_recving_` are all
guarded by `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::mu_`.

| Event | Scopes | Between them |
|---|---|---|
| `startRead`, `registerRecv`, `notifyForRead`, `sweepRecv`, `sweepSend` | 1 outer `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::mu_` scope (`StartRead(remote_endpoint)`, `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked` inside `RegisterRecv`, `NotifyForRead`, or `CompleteReadWithDetails`), nesting the incumbent or new session's `mu_` (`Done()`, `IsDraining()`, `IsReadyToComplete()`, `Finish()`, `GetStatus()`, `tracks_completion()`, `Details()`, `Create` / `AllocateStagingForLoad` / `InitFromLoadPlan`; the entry's `req_id` is read under manager `mu_` alone) and `StagingBlockAllocator::mu_` | `NotifyForRead` constructs the new `TransferSendSession` before taking manager `mu_` and calls its `Start()` (a no-op for a send) after releasing it; `StartRead` and `RegisterRecv` call the seated receive's `Start()` after releasing manager `mu_` (`Recv.initLoad` already counts the handshake op, see `PeerIsolation.lean`); `Done()` is monotone once true; and any candidate rejected by `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked` releases its staging slot (`~TransferReceiveSession`) before manager `mu_` is unlocked, preserving `freeSlots + activeStaging recvTable = cfg.numSlots` across the outer scope |
| `recvStep`, `sendStep` | per-session `TransferReceiveSession::mu_` and `TransferSendSession::mu_` scopes (`Receive.lean`, `Send.lean`) | see `Receive.lean` and `Send.lean` §"Lock scopes" |

## Main results

- **Resource conservation & session invariants (`reachable_inv`,
  `reachable_recv_safe`, `reachable_send_safe`):**
  `freeSlots + activeStaging recvTable = cfg.numSlots` holds on every reachable
  state (relying on `Recv.StagingIntegrity`: an entry is only erased or
  retired inline when `done = true`, at which point `hasStaging = false`; the
  one finish a registration performs on a ready incumbent returns the slot
  exactly when it settles it, `freedBy`), and every active entry satisfies
  `Recv.Safe` / `Send.Safe`.
- **Drain-before-reuse persistence (`active_recv_preserved`,
  `active_send_preserved`):**
  While an incumbent receive at `uuid` has `life.done = false` and either work
  in flight (`0 < life.inFlight`) or nothing the poll would finish
  (`¬ isReadyToComplete`), no enabled event (`startRead`, `registerRecv`,
  `notifyForRead`, `sweepRecv`, `sweepSend`, `recvStep`, `sendStep`) can remove
  it or change its `(reqId, gen)` — a registration may start it draining
  (`recv->Finish()` in `EmplaceRecvSessionLocked`) but cannot replace it until
  its last operation ends. The one incumbent a registration does replace in a
  single call is a ready receive with nothing in flight, which the finish
  settles on the spot (`trace_register_recv_replaces_ready_incumbent`, on the
  zero-layer receive of `ReceivePoll.lean`;
  `trace_register_recv_finishes_ready_incumbent` shows the window case, where
  an operation is still in flight and the incumbent stays). While a send offer at `uuid` has `life.done = false`,
  nothing removes it: `startRead` under its uuid fails into `failedRecving`,
  `registerRecv` and `notifyForRead` are refused.
